  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ProFoE-WA: Protecting Freedom of Expression in West Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the rapid spread of mis/disinformation, now amplified by generative AI; limited platform responsiveness to African languages and contexts; and evolving legal frameworks that risk criminalising legitimate online expression under broadly defined cybersecurity and false information policies and laws, Penplusbytes introduces the &apos;Protecting Freedom of Expression in West Africa&apos; project. 

The overall objective of the project is to strengthen the protection and exercise of freedom of expression (online and offline) in Ghana, Sierra Leone, Liberia, and Togo by enhancing early mis/disinformation detection mechanisms, building community resilience, and supporting evidence-based legal and policy reform. The specific objectives of the project are as follows:

SO1 - Detection and Evidence: Strengthen early detection and analysis of disinformation through coordinated, multilingual monitoring and country-level reporting.

SO2 - Community Resilience: Build the capacity of 10,000+ citizens, particularly women and young people, to identify, resist and counter disinformation through locally adapted community engagement (pre-bunking). Over 10,000 citizens will be directly reached through community activities such as the &#x201c;Caravan of Hope&#x201d; (25 community events in 4 countries), gaining awareness and foundational media and information literacy. This also encompasses 80 community ambassadors that will be trained across the 4 countries to sustain our interventions and provide mentorship support in their communities.

SO3 - Policy and Legal Reform: Promote a more enabling legal and regulatory environment for freedom of expression through research, multi-stakeholder dialogue, and evidence-based advocacy.</narrative>
  </description>
